# What every range's width is made of. One row per narrowing statement in every loaded document,
# classified into the thing that would actually reduce it.
#
# Ignorance or variation
#   The question this answers, only because `narrowsWhen` carries a kind. How much of the
#   uncertainty in the filings is ignorance, where a better instrument reveals the number that was
#   always there, and how much is the world actually moving, where no measurement helps and only
#   changing the process does? With no kind to group by, a schema asserts the first reading
#   everywhere, which is the assumption that makes people buy instruments for variation problems.
#
# `absent/reason = none` is variation too
#   It is the second way to say variation. "Somebody looked and nothing would narrow this" is not
#   missing information; it is a finding, and it belongs with `intervention` rather than with the
#   rows nobody has considered.
#
# A derivation is neither
#   A third reading. The width is not in the world at all: it follows from the widths of the terms
#   an identity works the claim out from, so nothing needs measuring and nothing needs changing, and
#   a receiver holding the terms already has it. A `booked` share under a clearance is the nameplate
#   less the demand, so it narrows exactly as far as the demand does and never further, and it names
#   `sharesSum`.
#   Left unfiled, a computed width gets said in prose instead and typed `instrument` (a width made
#   of ignorance that a better instrument reveals), when no instrument is involved and nothing is
#   unmeasured.
#
# The rows are scattered
#   They sit across demands, nameplates, quanta, slacks, shares, factors and coupling strengths,
#   because `narrowsWhen` sits on `Claim` and claims are everywhere. Gathering them makes the
#   question answerable at the level of a document.
#
# The filer's answer beside the measured width
#   It carries the element and the measured width beside the filer's own answer, which turns a
#   census into something checkable. `no range to narrow` in the CASE below is the filer saying so;
#   `is_a_point` is the arithmetic. Two rules compare them.
-- pm:Claim/pm:narrowsWhen, wherever a claim appears.
SELECT n.filing, n.seq, n.owns, n.is_a_point, n.low, n.high, n.unit,
       n.narrows_kind AS kind, n.narrows_absent AS absent, n.narrows_condition AS condition,
       CASE
         WHEN n.narrows_kind = 'instrument'      THEN 'ignorance: measure it better'
         WHEN n.narrows_kind = 'intervention'    THEN 'variation: only changing the process helps'
         WHEN n.narrows_kind = 'experiment'      THEN 'unknown, deliberately: an experiment would say'
         WHEN n.narrows_absent = 'none'
              THEN 'variation: somebody looked, nothing would narrow it'
         WHEN n.narrows_absent = 'notApplicable' THEN 'no range to narrow (a point value)'
         WHEN n.narrows_derivation IS NOT NULL
              THEN format('computed: it narrows as the terms of `%s` do', n.narrows_derivation)
         ELSE 'nobody has said'
       END AS what_the_width_is_made_of,
       n.narrows_derivation AS derivation
FROM (
    :compose(epistemics/claims.sqlc)
) n
